## Decisions

### How should the existing 107 recordings get moved over, now that a tool in `local/` won't survive the merge?

**Background.** After this change, each person or family has two recording columns:
- `pronunciation_original`: new and private. It holds the file exactly as uploaded.
- `pronunciation`: the file people play. The server makes it from the original as an AAC M4A, mono, 48 kHz, 64 kbps.

Today 85 `PERSON` rows and 22 family `GROUP` rows have a `pronunciation` but nothing in the new column (61 MP3s and 2 M4As in `gs://heliosian-media/pronunciation/`). Each of them has to have its current file copied into `pronunciation_original` once, so the server remakes the playable file from it.

My plan was the one-off tool `local/pronunciationoriginals`, run after the deploy. As you said, `local/` is untracked, so the merge deletes the tool with the worktree.

**Example row:** `peryDHPDJfsedP` has `pronunciation = pronunciation/4fa35602….mp3` (MP3, 3.72 s) and `pronunciation_original` empty. After the move it should have `pronunciation_original = pronunciation/4fa35602….mp3`, then `pronunciation = pronunciation/<new>.m4a` (AAC mono 48 kHz, 3.73 s, ~30 KB) once the worker remakes it.

- (*) The server adopts it at start
  When the new server starts and queues work for the photo-and-recording worker, a row with a `pronunciation` but no `pronunciation_original` is written as one batch, with `pronunciation_original` set to that file and `pronunciation` blanked. The worker then remakes each recording. About 8 lines in `Pictures.Start`, plus a test that starts from a row in the old shape.
  - For `peryDHPDJfsedP`: the first boot of the new revision sets `pronunciation_original = pronunciation/4fa35602….mp3`, and a fraction of a second later `pronunciation = pronunciation/<new>.m4a`.
  - There is no step for you to run. It also closes the delete gap the reviewer raised: by the time anyone can press delete, every row has an original.
  - The code stays after the move as a permanent rule: a recording with no original becomes its own original. Once the move is done no row matches, but it would also catch a `pronunciation` someone typed into the sheet by hand.
- ( ) I copy the tool into your main checkout
  I copy `local/pronunciationoriginals` to `~/work/heliosian/heliosian/local/`, and you run `go run ./local/pronunciationoriginals` there after the deploy. No server code changes.
  - For `peryDHPDJfsedP`: same result, but only once you run it. Until then the row has no original, so pressing delete on it leaves the old recording in place.
  - This means I write into a checkout outside this task, and you have a manual step after the deploy.

